@extends('layouts.app')

@section('content')
<div class="container docs-shell">
    @include('partials.docs-side')
    <article class="docs-body">
        <h1>Authentication</h1>
        <p>A session guard stores <code class="inline">login_id</code> after a successful attempt. Passwords are hashed with bcrypt (default) or argon2id via <code class="inline">Hash.make</code> / <code class="inline">Hash.check</code>. The default user provider reads the <code class="inline">users</code> table.</p>

        <h2>Login and logout</h2>
        <pre><code>Route.post("/login") { request ->
    val ok = Auth.attempt(mapOf(
        "email" to request.string("email"),
        "password" to request.string("password")
    ), remember = true)
    if (ok) redirect("/dashboard") else redirect("/login")
}

Route.post("/logout") {
    Auth.logout()
    redirect("/")
}</code></pre>

        <h2>The current user</h2>
        <pre><code>request.user()
Auth.check()
user()?.getAuthIdentifier()</code></pre>
        <p><code class="inline">./kotlimo new</code> writes register, login, logout, remember-me, and password reset. Remember-me stores a SHA-256 hash in <code class="inline">users.remember_token</code> and a <code class="inline">kotlimo_remember</code> cookie. Password reset emails a token through the mail driver and checks it against <code class="inline">password_resets</code>.</p>

        <h2>API tokens</h2>
        <pre><code>val plain = Auth.createToken(user, "mobile")
// Authorization: Bearer &lt;plain&gt;
Auth.user()
Auth.revokeToken(plain)</code></pre>
        <p>The bearer guard runs before the session guard. Tokens live in <code class="inline">personal_access_tokens</code> as SHA-256 hashes. Requests that send <code class="inline">Authorization: Bearer</code> skip CSRF.</p>

        <h2>Policies</h2>
        <pre><code>Gate.policy(Post::class, PostPolicy())
Gate.authorize(Auth.user(), "create", Post())</code></pre>
        <p><code class="inline">Gate.authorize</code> throws 403 when the policy denies the ability. Generate a policy with <code class="inline">make:policy PostPolicy</code>.</p>
    </article>
</div>
@endsection
